    "UIData_ShowProblem_eZys": "VIP Advanced Data",
    "UIData_ShowProblem_SM0y": "Total hands: hands played in the product.\\n\\nTotal games: games played in the product.\\n\\nVPIP: share of hands you voluntarily call or raise pre-flop (antes do not count). VPIP hands / total hands.\\n\\nVPIP win rate: share of VPIP hands won.\\n\\nAverage result: total result / total games.\\n\\nAverage buy-in: total buy-in / total games.",
    "UIData_ShowProblem_3xqp": "VPIP: share of hands in which you voluntarily put chips in the pot pre-flop. It measures how loose or tight you play.\\n\\nPFR: share of hands in which you raise pre-flop. PFR = pre-flop raises / pre-flop entries.\\n\\n3-bet: share of hands in which you re-raise after a bet or raise. 3-bet = re-raises / entries.\\n\\nC-bet: a bet on this street after you were the last aggressor on the previous street. C-bet = continuation bets / previous-street aggression.\\n\\nAF: higher means more aggressive (more bets/raises). AF = {\uFF08\u4E0B\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570+\u52A0\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570\uFF09/\u8DDF\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570}/50 (divide by 50 to show a percentage; capped at 100%, so the raw maximum is 50).\\n\\nWTSD: share of flopped hands that go to showdown. WTSD = showdown hands / flopped hands.\\n\\nAll-in Wins: win rate after going all-in. A high value usually means fewer bluff all-ins.\\n\\nVPIP Wins: win rate in hands that went to the pot.",
