    "UIData_Terminola9XjGbUJ": "Basic Data",
    "UIData_TerminolQ6ILftIz": "Total hands: The hands player used to play in ALL-IN.\\n\\nTotal games: The games player used to play in ALL-IN. \\n\\nVPIP: The ratio player ever raises or calls before flop in total hands. \\n\\nWins: The ratio player wins after raising or calling before flop in total hands.\\n\\nAvg result: The average achievement of all games played. \\n\\nAvg buy-in: The average buy-in of all games played.",
    "UIData_TerminolD6qL3kUc": "VIP Data",
    "UIData_TerminolbazUAGg6": "PFR: share of hands in which you raise pre-flop. PFR = pre-flop raises / pre-flop entries.\\n\\n3-bet: share of hands in which you re-raise after a bet or raise. 3-bet = re-raises / entries.\\n\\nC-bet: a bet on this street after you were the last aggressor on the previous street. C-bet = continuation bets / previous-street aggression.\\n\\nAF: higher means more aggressive (more bets/raises). AF = {\uFF08\u4E0B\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570+\u52A0\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570\uFF09/\u8DDF\u6CE8\u7684\u6B21\u6570}/50 (divide by 50 to show a percentage; capped at 100%, so the raw maximum is 50).\\n\\nWTSD: share of flopped hands that go to showdown. WTSD = showdown hands / flopped hands.\\n\\nAll-in Wins: win rate after going all-in. A high value usually means fewer bluff all-ins.",
