    "UITexasRule_Introduce": "<b><size=50>Introduction</size></b>\\nTexas Hold'em, which began in the early 20th century in Texas, is the most popular public poker game in Europe and America with a history of hundreds of years. Texas Hold'em is a poker game favored by chess and card lovers all over the world.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Gameplay</size></b>\\n1.There are four rounds in Texas Hold'em;\\n2.Pre-flop: each player will be dealt with 2 cards and then start the first round;\\n3.Flop: after the three community cards are dealt, the remaining players from the first round will start the second round;\\n4.Turn: the third round after the 4th community card is dealt;\\n5.River: the fourth round after the 5th community card is dealt;\\n6.After the game is over, all remaining players must show their cards and the player with the highest hand wins the pot.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Ranking of poker hand:</size></b>\\nRoyal Flush>Straight Flush>Four of a kind>Full House>Flush>Straight>Three of a kind>Two Pairs>One Pair>High Card\\nRanking of the card: \\nA>K>Q>J>10>9>8>7>6>5>4>3>2, regardless of suit\\n\\n",
    "UIPlO4Rule_Introduce": "<b><size=50>Introduction</size></b>\\nOmaha is very similar to Texas Hold\u2019em with one game-changing factor. Instead of two hand cards, each player is dealt four to six cards. In Omaha, players must make the best possible hand with a combination that two from their hand cards and three from the community cards.\\n\\n<b><size=50>PLO4</size></b>\\nIn Pot Limit Omaha (the most popular form of Omaha Poker), the maximum a player can put stacks is the same amount as in the pot. \u201C4\u201D means four cards will be dealt to each player.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Gameplay</size></b>\\n1. There are four rounds in Omaha;\\n2.Pre-flop: each player will be dealt with 4 cards and then start the first round;\\n3.Flop: After the three community cards are dealt, the remaining players from the first round will start the second round;\\n4.Turn the third round after the 4th community card is dealt;\\n5.River: the fourth round after the 5th community card is dealt;\\n6.After the game is over, all remaining players must show their cards and the player with the highest hand wins the pot.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Ranking of poker hand:</size></b>\\nRoyal Flush>Straight Flush>Four of a kind>Full House>Flush>Straight>Three of a kind>Two Pairs>One Pair>High Card\\nRanking of the card: \\nA>K>Q>J>10>9>8>7>6>5>4>3>2, regardless of suit\\n\\n",
    "UIPlO5Rule_Introduce": "<b><size=50>Introduction</size></b>\\nOmaha is very similar to Texas Hold\u2019em with one game changing factor. Instead of two hand cards, each player is dealt four to six cards. In Omaha, players must make the best possible hand with a combination that two from their hand cards and three from the community cards.\\n\\n<b><size=50>PLO5</size></b>\\nIn Pot Limit Omaha (most popular form of Omaha Poker), the maximum a player can put UC is as the same amount as in the pot. \u201C5\u201D means five cards will be dealt to each player.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Gameplay</size></b>\\n1.There are four betting rounds in Omaha;\\n2.Pre-flop: each player will be dealt with 5 cards and then start the first round;\\n3.Flop: after the three community cards are dealt, the remaining players from the first round will start the second round;\\n4.Turn: the third round after the 4th community card is dealt;\\n5.River: the fourth round after the 5th community card is dealt;\\n6.After the game is over, all remaining players must show their cards and the player with the highest hand wins the pot.\\n\\n<b><size=50>Ranking of poker hand:</size></b>\\nRoyal Flush>Straight Flush>Four of a kind>Full House>Flush>Straight>Three of a kind>Two Pairs>One Pair>High Card\\nRanking of the card: \\nA>K>Q>J>10>9>8>7>6>5>4>3>2, regardless of suit\\n\\n",
    "UIPlO6Rule_Introduce": "<b><size=46>Introduction</size></b>\\nOmaha is very similar to Texas Hold\u2019em with one game changing factor. Instead of two hand cards, each player is dealt four to six cards. In Omaha, players must make the best possible hand with a combination that two from their hand cards and three from the community cards.\\n\\n<b><size=46>PLO6</size></b>\\nIn Pot Limit Omaha (most popular form of Omaha Poker), the maximum a player can put stacks is as the same amount as in the pot. \u201C6\u201D means six cards will be dealt to each player.\\n\\n<b><size=46>Gameplay</size></b>\\n1.There are four rounds in Omaha;\\n2.Pre-flop: each player will be dealt with 6 cards and then start the first round;\\n3.Flop: after the three community cards are dealt, the remaining players from the first round will start the second round;\\n4.Turn: the third round after the 4th community card is dealt;\\n5.River: the fourth round after the 5th community card is dealt;\\n6.After the game is over, all remaining players must show their cards and the player with the highest hand wins the pot.\\n\\n<b><size=46>Ranking of poker hand:</size></b>\\nRoyal Flush>Straight Flush>Four of a kind>Full House>Flush>Straight>Three of a kind>Two Pairs>One Pair>High Card\\nRanking of the card: \\nA>K>Q>J>10>9>8>7>6>5>4>3>2, regardless of suit\\n\\n",
    "UI6Plus_Introduce": "<b><size=46>6+ Hold'em</size></b>\\n6+ Hold'em is a popular \u201Cshort deck\u201D poker gameplay\xA0that mostly follows the same rules with Texas Hold\u2019em, but with a few exciting differences:\\n1.All cards lower than 6 are removed from the deck;\\n2.Everyone put UC and only the button blind - known as the \u201Cbutton blind\u201D;\\n3.Flush beats Full-house and A, 6, 7, 8, 9 is classified as lowest straight\\nAvailable exclusively at NEW POKER, 6+ Hold\u2019em gives you the chance to play an action-packed gameplay loved by high-stakes players around the world.\\n\\n",
