    "UIMushRule": "Pile Mushrooms Play Rules: \\n1\u3001Pile Mushrooms is a variant of the [NLH] [PLO] [6+] game, where the Dealer player in each hand is the Mushroom Seeder, and the SB (Small Blind) player is the Mushroom Snatcher; \\n2. In each hand, the Dealer puts a mushroom (the amount of stacks corresponding to 1 mushroom is fixed during the table creation) into the mushroom pot before the flop, and the Mushroom pot begins to accumulate; \\n3. In the Pile Mushrooms game, the Dealer position puts a mushroom Pre-flop in each hand, which is automatic and mandatory; \\n4. If the SB player wins, he will get all the mushroom rewards from the mushroom pot; \\n5\u3001After the mushroom pot has been obtained by SB, it means that this round of mushroom play is over, and the pot will start accumulating again and a new round of mushroom play will be opened; \\n6\u3001A new player joins, he can participate in the game normally, but he does not participate in the Pile Mushrooms, The Dealer does not need to put mushrooms into the pot when it is his turn to play, and SB can not be awarded for his victory, and he needs to wait for the new round of Pile Mushrooms \\n\\n",
