    "UIEgg_Record": "Guandan Records",
    "UIEgg": "Guandan",
    "UICreateRoom_Egg": "Guandan Table",
    "UIEgg_LevelCardModel": "Trump Card Mode",
    "UIEgg_LevelCardModelTwo": "Tribute starts from level 2",
    "UIEgg_LevelCardModelRandom": "Random no tribute each game",
    "UIEgg_GameRule": "Game Rules",
    "UIEgg_AllowDoubling": "Double Allowed",
    "UIEgg_Scorer": "Scoreboard",
    "UIEgg_RemainDisplay": "Show when 10 cards left",
    "UIEgg_GameRuleTips": "Allow Doubling: after the deal, each player may double or not; one double multiplies by 2.\\nCard Counter: shows remaining-card counts on the table.\\nShow at 10 Cards: hand counts stay hidden until a player has 10 or fewer cards.",
    "UIAutoChangeTable1": "Please change the configuration.",
    "UIAutoChangeTable2": "At anti-cheating tables, when the number of hands played reaches the threshold, players will be randomly reassigned to new tables.",
    "UIAutoChangeTable3": "Current table will reshuffle after participating in {0} hands.",
    "UIAutoChangeTable4": "Auto Table Change",
    "UIAutoChangeTable5": "Will automatically switch to a new table after this hand ends.",
    "UIEgg_TwoRate": "Second Finisher Rate",
    "UIEgg_AddRate": "Double",
    "UIEgg_PressRate": "Average Suppression per Game",
    "UIEgg_HeadRate": "First Finisher Rate",
    "UIEgg_TwoRateTips": "Cooperation: Percentage of all hands in which the player finishes second.",
    "UIEgg_AddRateTips": "Aggressive: Ratio of hands in which the player chose to double.",
    "UIEgg_PressRateTips": "Suppressive: Number of times per hand the player suppresses opponents.",
    "UIEgg_HeadRateTips": "Independent: Percentage of all hands in which the player finishes first.",
    "UICreateSNGPlayerNumberError": "For games with more than 9 players, the number must be a multiple of 9.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_1": "Guandan is 2v2. Each game has a level card, the highest rank after the jokers. Heart level cards are wild. Your opposite seat is your partner. The first side to empty its hands wins, and that finish sets the settlement multiplier.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_2": "Card Type Introduction:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_3": "Bomb:\\nFour or more cards of the same rank form a bomb. A bomb beats every non-bomb and any smaller bomb.\\nThe two Heart wilds can join any number of the same rank to make a bomb; strength follows the finished length.\\nLonger bombs beat shorter ones; equal length is ranked by point.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_4": "Straight flush:\\nFive consecutive cards of one suit. Highest is 10-J-Q-K-A; lowest is A-2-3-4-5. A straight flush beats every non-bomb hand.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_5": "Straight:\\nExactly five consecutive singles, such as A-2-3-4-5 or 10-J-Q-K-A. Beaten by a straight flush or a bomb.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_6": "Consecutive pairs:\\nThree or more consecutive pairs, such as 334455 or JJQQKKAA. Ranked by the highest pair.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_7": "Triple sequence with pairs:\\nTwo or more consecutive triples with the same number of pairs, such as 333+44 or 777+888+99. Compare triples first, then pairs.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_8": "Single, pair, triple, triple+1, triple+pair:\\nThese basic types beat one another by rank, high to low.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_9": "Tractor (some regions):\\nTwo or more consecutive pairs in the same suit, such as 4455 or 778899. Ranked by the highest pair.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_10": "Card Comparison Rules:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_11": "Between bombs:\\nMore cards beat fewer; equal length is ranked by point.\\nJoker bomb > 6+ bomb > straight flush > 5-or-fewer bomb > other hands",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_12": "Non-bomb hands:\\nSame type, same length: higher rank wins.\\nDifferent types: bomb beats all non-bombs; a straight flush beats a straight and other non-bombs; a straight beats other non-bombs; and so on.\\nJokers > level cards > A",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_13": "Special Cases:\\n If a wildcard is used in a combination (e.g., to form a bomb), its value depends on the resulting hand it helps create.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_14": "Final score:\\nThe winning side is paid from the table stake and multiplier. Each of the two losers pays half to the two winners.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_15": "Scoring rule is: Base Points \xD7 Hand Multiplier \xD7 Ranking Multiplier",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_16": "Hand Multipliers 4-card bomb \xD7 2, 5-card bomb \xD7 3, Straight flush \xD7 4, 6+ card bomb \xD7 5, Joker bomb \xD7 6:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_17": "Ranking Multipliers\u201CFirst out\u201D and \u201CSecond out\u201D \xD7 6, \u201CThird out\u201D \xD7 3, \u201CLast out\u201D \xD7 1:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_18": "Trump Card Rules:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_19": "Level cards:\\nThe current game level can be any rank from 2 to A in every suit. The series starts at 2 and moves up after each promotion. At level 3, every 3 (including Heart 3) is a level card.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_20": "What level cards do:\\nTrump: any suit of the level card outranks the same type of non-trump (singles, pairs, consecutive pairs, triples, and so on).\\nSpecial hands: they can also form tractors (consecutive level pairs) or straight flushes (same-suit level runs), which are very strong.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_21": "Promotion:\\nRank is updated after each game from the partnership finish. First and second (double-up) promote 3 levels; first and third promote 2; first and last promote 1. The other side drops by the same amount.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_22": "After each game the next level card follows the promotion. A side that leaves level 3 plays level 4 next, and so on up to A.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_23": "Heart level cards:\\nIn Guandan they are also wild. A Heart level card can stand for any card except the jokers, so at level 3 Heart 3 can complete a tractor or straight flush.\\nThey are sometimes called \u201Cmatch any\u201D because they can pair with other cards to make stronger combinations.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_24": "Tribute Rules:",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_25": "Top 2 are winners (\u201CFirst out\u201D and \u201CSecond out\u201D), bottom 2 are losers (\u201CThird\u201D and \u201CLast\u201D).",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_26": "Tribute:\\nLosers tribute to winners.\\nDouble-down (3rd and 4th): each loser tributes their highest non-Heart-trump card. The higher card goes to first-out, the lower to second-out.\\nSingle-down (only one last): last-out tributes their highest non-Heart-trump card to first-out.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_27": "Refuse tribute:\\nIf both big jokers sit with one or both losers, the losing side may refuse tribute.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_28": "Which card to tribute:\\nTribute your highest card. If several non-trump cards tie for highest, choose one. If the highest is a non-Heart level card, tribute that. If the highest is a joker and refuse-tribute does not apply, tribute the joker.",
    "UIEgg_GameRule_29": "Return tribute:\\nFirst-out and, when needed, second-out each return one card of their choice. It is usually a weak card and must not be a current trump.",
    "UIEgg_Prepare": "Prepare",
    "UIEgg_Friend": "Teammate",
    "UIEgg_Enemy": "Opponent",
    "UIEgg_NotOut": "Pass",
